## Work log

### towel-stack-b — commit 3dfd1518

- 5 `./forge render --fast` passes and 1 `./forge inspect --fast`.
- The first pass read as three flat plates. The passes after it rounded the fold edges, rebuilt
  the hanging corner as a two-part flap (one on the top surface, one over the front edge), moved
  the stitch band to the top surface, deepened the press dent, and set the stack height to 0.22 m.
- Inspect: no floating part, no buried part, lowest point y = 0.
- Mech-check: `{"asset":"towel-stack-b","ok":true,"forgeAll":{"exitCode":0,"warnings":[]},"triangles":1052,"bottomY":0,"files":{"glb":true,"stats":true,"render":true,"sprites":true,"glbBytes":1352712},"typecheckExit":0,"failures":[]}`
- Card: `out/hy4-trial/cards/r1/towel-stack-b.png`. The card and the sprite preview were read once.

### wash-basin-b — commit 6a03ea7e

- 6 `./forge render --fast` passes and 2 `./forge inspect --fast` runs.
- The first pass showed a lumpy rim. The passes after it widened the cavity so the water reads,
  moved the sawn stave tops from wide blocks to a scalloped crown with small pegs, faded the
  stave lobes under the rim, and gave the basin a finer mesh (detail 0.0065, 4200 triangles)
  because the rim tube was only two cells across and the reduction lumped it.
- The first mech-check failed on the type check (4 errors: `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` on the
  `wallRadius` table). The table reads changed; the geometry did not. The mech-check then passed.
- Inspect: no floating part, no buried part, lowest point y = 0.
- Mech-check: `{"asset":"wash-basin-b","ok":true,"forgeAll":{"exitCode":0,"warnings":[]},"triangles":5910,"bottomY":0,"files":{"glb":true,"stats":true,"render":true,"sprites":true,"glbBytes":2716880},"typecheckExit":0,"failures":[]}`
- Card: `out/hy4-trial/cards/r1/wash-basin-b.png`. The card and the sprite preview were read once.

### towel-rack-a — commit 38f93cb5

- 4 `./forge render --fast` passes and 4 `./forge inspect --fast` runs.
- The passes fixed the stretcher length (it floated between the legs), the peg (it was hidden
  by the hand towel), the leg thickness, and the wide towel (the front panel became an extruded
  cloth outline with uneven sides and a wavy hem instead of a flat box).
- Inspect: no floating part, no buried part, lowest point y = -0.004 m. The iron peg was under
  0.3% of the silhouette in the last inspect, so the peg grew a longer shaft and a bigger head.
- Mech-check: `{"asset":"towel-rack-a","ok":true,"forgeAll":{"exitCode":0,"warnings":[]},"triangles":4804,"bottomY":-0.004,"files":{"glb":true,"stats":true,"render":true,"sprites":true,"glbBytes":1773764},"typecheckExit":0,"failures":[]}`
- Card: `out/hy4-trial/cards/r1/towel-rack-a.png`. The card and the sprite preview were read once.

## Step limit

The role hit its step limit after `wash-basin-b` and the orchestrator continued the same try
(round 1, not a new try) with the same rules and the same base. The work order after the
continuation was: 2 more `--fast` passes and the mech-check for `wash-basin-b`, then 4 passes
and the mech-check for `towel-rack-a`, then this plan sub-bullet and this log block in one
commit. The render and the inspect ran as one heavy job per asset; the mech-check and the card
ran as one heavy job per asset.

## Known misses of arm 2 round 1

- towel-stack-b: the press dent in the top of the stack reads weakly; the stitch band edge is
  slightly ragged; the hanging corner reads as a narrow tab rather than a wide folded corner.
- wash-basin-b: the pale rim band still reads a little wavy; the staves read more as a basket
  weave than as separate blocks; the front view alone can read as a planter; the water shows in
  the three-quarter and top views but not from a level camera.
- towel-rack-a: the teal hem is one band where the mockup has three; the legs are slimmer than
  the mockup's; the hand towel is small; the wide towel still reads partly as a flat panel above
  its wavy hem.

